 and metallic powder alloys, as well as long product forms, such as ingot, billet, bar, rod, wire, shapes and rectangles, seamless tubes, plus precision forgings, components, and machined parts. It also offers zirconium and related alloys, including hafnium and niobium, nickel-based alloys, titanium and titanium-based alloys, and specialty alloys in various forms, such as plate, sheet, and precision rolled strip products. In addition, the company provides hot-rolling conversion services comprising carbon steel products. It serves medical and specialty energy, aerospace and defense, construction and mining, transportation, oil and gas, automotive, food equipment and appliances, and mining markets. The company was formerly known as Allegheny Technologies Incorporated. ATI Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Kimberly A. Fields | President, CEO & Chair | Age 55 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $604K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $44K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["ATI Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $24.9B market cap on $4.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 10% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $334M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 237% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.372835522611098},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $49.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ATI (NYSE:ATI) Stock Price Expected to Rise, BTIG Research Analyst Says","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/ati-nyseati-stock-price-expected-to-rise-btig-research-analyst-says.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577379.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Missed ATI's 91% Gain? Here's What Investors Got Right","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-ati/ati/news/missed-atis-91-gain-heres-what-investors-got-right","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569182.639,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.372,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ATI Targets $7 Billion by 2029, Sees More Runway in Aerospace and Defense","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ati-targets-7-billion-2029-101436997.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794564876.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ATI Announces 2029 Financial Goals and Expands Nickel Powder and Zirconium Sponge Production","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/ati-announces-2029-financial-goals-and-expands-nickel-powder-and-zirconium-sponge-production","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794512974.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ATI Unveils Acceleration Strategy, Targets Double-Digit Growth and Expanded Margins","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/ati-unveils-accel